[medium, design/efficiency] gix-store/src/index.rs:24-53 + kind.rs:372-378 — the index never saves a read. read_validated only returns the decoded index when it is exactly equal to the freshly-scanned source, and list_entries computes source_entries() (the full ref scan) before consulting it. So the cached result is by construction identical to what the caller already has: every list pays scan + index-ref read + tree decode + comparison, strictly more work than having no index. Locally the index is pure overhead on both read and write paths; if its purpose is external consumers reading refs/cache directly (git-query?), say so in a comment — otherwise reads should be able to trust the index without re-scanning, or the index should go. Also the entries.iter().all(|(name,_)| entities.join_path(name).is_under(entities)) check at index.rs:45-47 is tautological — join_path under a prefix is always under that prefix — and can be dropped.
